Package: swbrd-turnserver
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Evan Brass <brassevan@gmail.com>
Section: net
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: swbrd-common (>= @COMPAT@), nginx (>= 1.26), libnginx-mod-stream, nftables, systemd, init-system-helpers (>= 1.54), libc6 (>= 2.38), libgcc-s1
Suggests: certbot
Homepage: https://github.com/evan-brass/swbrd
Description: Stateless TURN relay using the TURN wire format over UDP
 Relays for WebRTC clients without keeping allocation state, encoding the
 allocation into an IPv6 address instead.  Ships the nginx stream configuration
 that terminates turns: on 5349 and multiplexes TLS, HTTP and ssh on 443, plus
 the per-client nftables accounting for the :3478 sockets.
 .
 Built for one private host and not fit for redistribution; see
 /usr/share/doc/swbrd-turnserver/copyright.
